  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This idea is simple. Eventually when VRChat is published to mobile and no longer in early access. There should be a cardboard mode in VRChat. Back in the old days of VR, phones were the first capable device to show the intricate details VR can provide to the masses.\n\nBy connecting a supported physical controller such as Xbox or PlayStation controller, or other 3rd party. And buying a Cardboard made headset that's still buildable or findable on Amazon and other hobby sites that keep this idea alive. There should be a way on supported phones to keep the screen split on each eye with plastic lenses.\n\nThe idea I thought of would be suitable to anyone who doesn't have the affordance of buying a full VR rig whether it be via PC with multiple branded cabled headsets, or just straight-up Meta Quest.\n\nIf this idea sounds good, I would love to hear it! Thank you for reading! <3",
